    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0600" n="494" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg494"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Squiers to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-09-01"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 1, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1321.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    department’s instructions No. 519<anchor n="a" xml:id="d437-f1"/> of July 14,
                    and No. 529<anchor n="a" xml:id="d437-f2"/> of July 29, with <pb facs="0601"
                        n="495" xml:id="pg495"/> reference to the Cuban trade-mark registration law,
                    and in reply to advise you that the matter was duly brought to the attention of
                    the Cuban Government with a view to correcting the abuses complained of.</p>
                <p>The Secretary of State has replied to my representations suggesting that the
                    United States join in the “treaty on patents of invention, industrial drawings,
                    and models and trade-marks,” a treaty that was considered during the second
                    conference which took place in Mexico in 1902, and to which President Palma
                    proposes Cuba shall subscribe.</p>
                <p>In inclosing a translation of this note I beg to say that I shall make no further
                    representations, awaiting your instructions.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. G. Squiers.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d437-a1.xml" xpointer="d437-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
